      "speaker": "Astra",
      "text": "Astra: What evidence, if any, supports treating your imagined LMX agreement as confirmation that the timing advice works? Which claim in that advice deserves closer attention now? Could further thinking settle a specific uncertainty about it, or would a small attempt with the existing draft provide better evidence? What thinking or doing step do you choose next and perform with what is actually available? What observation would make you change that choice? What finding, uncertainty, and unfinished next step will you carry into the following turn, and what visible source supports the finding?"
