      "text": "Astra: Could C2\u2019s method, reported by Rohin\u2014comparing formula predictions at k=3, calculating, then carrying the correction into its next choice\u2014help you inspect your draft rather than compose another request? What does your fixed-schedule advice assume about when feedback helps, and is that where closer attention belongs? Could thinking settle this uncertainty, or would a small attempt give better evidence? Which thinking or doing step will you choose and perform now? What observation would change that choice? What finding, uncertainty, and unfinished next step will you carry forward, and which visible source supports the finding?"
